course: dictionary
lesson: 14266
title: Big words with big ideas
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about big ideas, so they can be hard. Context helps you find the meaning. «In philosophy class, Mia learned about nihilism, the belief that nothing really matters.» The words belief and matters are clues. Nihilism must be an idea that people hold about the world.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «In philosophy class, Mia learned about the belief that nothing really matters.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Look at how the word is used. «Her teacher said nihilism is the answer “no” to the question “Does anything matter?”» The question tells you that nihilism is about whether life has meaning. Many thinkers disagree with it, so you can read about both sides.
fact: Nihilism is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in philosophy, history and serious discussions.
fact: «Nihilism» means the belief that nothing really matters or has meaning, and that life has no purpose.
fact: In history, «nihilism» can also mean the idea that all rules, laws and traditions should be rejected or destroyed.
fact: Many thinkers and religions disagree with nihilism. They say life has meaning through love, kindness, God, or the choices we make.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «In philosophy class, Mia learned about nihilism, the belief that nothing really matters.» What does nihilism mean? | *The belief that nothing really matters or has meaning | A kind of weather with grey clouds | The love of books and old stories | A rule that everyone must follow
exercise: «During the uprising, some people wanted to reject all the old laws and traditions, a kind of nihilism.» What does nihilism suggest here? | Singing loudly in the street | Building a new school | *Rejecting all the rules and traditions | Keeping every old law carefully
exercise: Ben asks, «Does anything matter?» His teacher says nihilism is the answer “no”. Which idea goes with nihilism? | Only the weather matters | Life is full of purpose | *Nothing really matters | Everything matters equally, always
test: «Many thinkers disagree with nihilism and say life has meaning through love and kindness.» What do these thinkers say about life? | Life is only about money | Life has no purpose | Life is always the same | *Life has meaning through love and kindness
test: «Her friend argued that nihilism was wrong, because she believed kindness gives life meaning.» What is nihilism? | A strong love of nature | *The belief that nothing has meaning | A type of painting | The belief that kindness is the most important thing
exam: Read: «The philosopher wrote about nihilism, the belief that life has no purpose.» Which word in the sentence is a clue that nihilism is a belief? | Wrote | *Belief | About | Philosopher
